$\mathrm{Cr}_2 \mathrm{O}_7^{2-}+14 \mathrmH^{+}+6 \mathrm{Fe}^{2+} \longrightarrow 2 \mathrm{Cr}^{3+}+6 \mathrm{Fe}^{3+}+7 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}$
no. of equivalents $\mathrm{K}_2 \mathrm{Cr}_2 \mathrm{O}_7=$ no. of equivalents $\mathrm{FeSO}_4\begin{aligned}
& \frac{1}{60} \times \mathrm{V} \times 6=1 \times 0.1 \times 100 \\
& \mathrm{ V}_{\mathrm{ml}}=10 \times 0.1 \times 100=100 \mathrm{ml} \\
& \mathrm{ V}_{\mathrm{in} \mathrm{ L}}=\frac{100}{1000}=0.1 \mathrm{ L}
\end{aligned}$

The balanced chemical equation is :-
$\begin{aligned}
& 6 \mathrm{Fe}^{2+} \text{ (aq.) }+14 \mathrm{H}^{+} \text{(aq.) }+\mathrm{Cr}_2 \mathrm{O}_7^{2-} \text{ (aq.) } \rightarrow \\
& 7 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O} \text{ (l) }+6 \mathrm{Fe}^{3+} \text{ (aq.) }+2 \mathrm{Cr}^{3+} \text{ (aq.) }
\end{aligned}$
Thus, $x=6, y=14 and z=1$

